Re: ANSI source

For the most part, there is an attempt to ANSIfy the nethack source.
Unfortunately, this is not upward compatible with old C compilers.
Since we don't want to keep all those folks with non-ANSI compilers from
playing, it gets to be a challange to support everything.  Then there's
those compilers that claim to be ANSI but aren't.

It would be a lot easier to make the source fully ANSIfied (with
#ifdef's, of course) if there were more compilers that groked ANSI.
And, just as importantly, system <.h> files that were in the correct
ANSI format, with the correct declarations of all the ANSI library
routines, including return values (name withheld to protect the guilty).

I've successfully compiled nethack with gcc w/o -traditional, so the
source isn't too far from being ANSI compliant.  No, I haven't compiled
w/-ansi.

